[{:adr/consequences ["capability-based cross-org organization is validated: the vertical-capability-lib sense (:required-technology-index) already exists as structured, machine-readable data across all 175 cloud-itonami blueprints, and needed only mining + cross-referencing, not invention" "13-keyword vocabulary is small and mostly clean: 8/13 keywords resolve cleanly to a registered kotoba-lang provider; 3/13 (audit-ledger, telemetry, optimization) have no provider at all; 1/13 (cae) has an ambiguous near-miss provider; 2 providers (bpmn, dmn) have a byte-identical unregistered -clj twin left over from the ADR-2606302300 migration" "the single highest-leverage unresolved item is :audit-ledger — required by literally every one of the 175 blueprints, with no canonical named home; the real implementation is already scattered across commit-dag/prolly-tree/kotobase-peer, so this is a naming/discoverability gap, not a from-scratch build" "a much larger, purely mechanical gap was found as a side effect: all 175 cloud-itonami-* blueprint repos are unregistered in west.yml; NOT acted on here because ~80 of them (the iso3166 sub-family) are mid-flight under an active /loop maturity-promotion process (ADR-2607040800/2607042900) and a concurrent wholesale registration risks racing it" "this ADR is descriptive/analytical only: no manifest edits, no repo retirements, no new scaffolding performed. Candidate follow-ups (register kotoba-lang/identity; retire com-junkawasaki/{bpmn,dmn}-clj; batch-register the 175 cloud-itonami blueprints once the iso3166 loop is confirmed idle; scope a :supply-chain-matching capability lib) are each independent, separately-approvable pieces of work, not bundled into this ADR"], :adr/authoritative_for ["disambiguation of the THREE distinct senses of \"capability\" already live in this superproject (runtime-security / labor-classification-tag / vertical-capability-lib) — see :capability-senses" "the mined :required-technology-index — 13 capability keywords used by all 175 cloud-itonami-* blueprint repos' blueprint.edn, each resolved (or flagged unresolved) against a canonical kotoba-lang provider repo" "concrete duplication finding: kotoba-lang/bpmn and kotoba-lang/dmn each have a byte-identical, unregistered, stale com-junkawasaki/{bpmn,dmn}-clj twin left over from the ADR-2606302300 migration" "concrete west-registration gap: all 175 local orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-* checkouts are unregistered in manifest/west.yml (only the private gftdcojp/cloud-itonami base repo is registered); kotoba-lang/identity (a required-technology provider used by 167/175 blueprints) is also unregistered despite being checked out" "does NOT extend the capability mining to etzhayyim (176 actors) or gftdcojp (60 products) in this pass — cloud-itonami's blueprint.edn was the only org with a uniform, machine-readable per-repo capability manifest at time of writing; etzhayyim's closest analog (:actor/labor ISIC/ISCO/UNSPSC tags) answers a different question (which human-labor vertical does this actor touch) and was not mined here" "does NOT perform any mutating action (no west registration, no repo retirement) — descriptive/analytical only, per owner instruction to do the capability-map analysis first"], :adr/capability-senses "[{:sense :runtime-security, :aka \"object-capability / EROS-KeyKos-style access control\", :answers-the-question \"what may this RUNNING code do right now (net/fs/graph/llm-infer/...)?\", :owning-repos [\"kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang\" \"kotoba-lang/aiueos\"], :authority [\"orgs/kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang/docs/adr/ADR-safe-capability-language.md\" \"90-docs/adr/2606290930-kotoba-aiueos-capability-bridge.md\" \"90-docs/adr/2606290900-kotoba-aiueos-key-lifecycle-revocation.md\"], :example \"kotoba.app.edn :requires #{:cap/kqe} (etzhayyim actor mesh-deployment manifest); typed grants graph/read, net/fetch, llm/infer\", :not-for-this-adr \"irrelevant to repo/portfolio organization; this is a per-call runtime permission model, not a classification of what a repo IS\"} {:sense :labor-classification-tag, :aka \"ISIC/ISCO/UNSPSC labor-displacement accounting tag\", :answers-the-question \"which human-labor industry/occupation/product vertical does this actor's work touch (for Displacement Dividend accounting)?\", :owning-repos [\"etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-*\"], :authority [\"orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-noroshi/manifest.edn :actor/labor\"], :example \"{:isic [\\\"C26\\\" \\\"C2620\\\" \\\"J61\\\"] :isco [\\\"2152\\\" \\\"7311\\\" \\\"8212\\\"] :unspsc [\\\"32\\\" \\\"41\\\" \\\"43\\\"]}\", :not-mined-this-pass \"answers a different question (whose labor, not which tech-dependency); would need its own pass across 176 etzhayyim actors, not attempted here\"} {:sense :vertical-capability-lib, :aka \"reusable technology-capability a product/blueprint declares it depends on\", :answers-the-question \"which named, reusable kotoba-lang module implements a function this blueprint needs (banking ledger, BPMN engine, audit trail, ...)?\", :owning-repos [\"kotoba-lang/{banking,swift,phone,card,retail,logistics,property,labor,robotics,insurance,securities,bpmn,dmn,forms,identity,industry,occupation,cofog,unspsc,iso3166}\" \"cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-<code> (consumer side, via blueprint.edn :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies)\"], :authority [\"ADR-2607011000\" \"ADR-2607012000\" \"ADR-2607032000\" \"manifest/repos.edn (\\\"vertical capability lib\\\" / \\\"capability registry\\\" comments)\"], :example \"cloud-itonami-6411/blueprint.edn :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :banking]\", :this-adr \"THIS is the sense :required-technology-index below generalizes across the whole cloud-itonami blueprint fleet\"}]", :adr/topic "cross-org-capability", :adr/related ["ADR-2606302300 (4-org taxonomy: what-kind-of-thing x for-whom axes; this ADR adds an ORTHOGONAL what-capability axis, does not change org placement)" "ADR-2607022800 (kotoba-lang-internal dependency map: 44 clusters + full adjacency graph; source of most canonical-provider lookups below)" "ADR-2606290930 (kotoba<->aiueos capability bridge) + ADR-safe-capability-language.md (kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang repo) — authority for the runtime-security sense of \"capability\", explicitly NOT the sense this ADR's :required-technology-index uses" "ADR-2607011000 (cloud-itonami robotics premise + ISIC-21-21 — origin of the ISIC-vertical-capability-lib pattern: swift/banking/phone/card/retail/logistics/property/labor/robotics)" "ADR-2607012000 (cloud-itonami-isco occupation blueprints), ADR-2607031600 (cofog), ADR-2607031700 (unspsc), ADR-2607032330 (iso3166), ADR-2607032000 (insurance/securities financial-services batch) — the other 4 classification-standard axes cloud-itonami blueprints are keyed on" "ADR-2607040800 + ADR-2607042900 (cloud-itonami-iso3166 maturity-promotion sweep 1 and 2, self-paced /loop) — the iso3166 sub-family is a KNOWN, actively-growing, in-progress roadmap item; this ADR's iso3166 numbers are a snapshot, not a gap report"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607051300-cross-org-capability-map", :adr/west-registration-gap "{:cloud-itonami-blueprint-repos {:total-unregistered 175, :registered 0, :note \"manifest/west.yml has exactly one cloud-itonami-related entry: name \\\"cloud-itonami\\\", path \\\"orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami\\\" — the PRIVATE business-os base repo (per ADR-2606302300's 2026-07-04 amendment). None of the 175 public cloud-itonami-<code> blueprint repos under the dedicated cloud-itonami GitHub org (per ADR-2607012100) have a west.yml entry at all.\", :scale-comparison \"35x the size of the 5-repo gap ADR-2607022800 gap-swept for kotoba-lang\", :caution \"do NOT batch-register all 175 blindly right now: the iso3166 sub-family (~80 of the 175) is mid-flight under a self-paced /loop maturity-promotion process (ADR-2607040800, ADR-2607042900) that lands its own commits in waves; a wholesale west sweep run concurrently risks racing that process. If/when this gap is closed, sequence it AFTER confirming the iso3166 loop is not currently running, and follow the same --entry-minimal-diff + server-side pin-verification discipline ADR-2607022800 used, not a wholesale regen.\"}, :kotoba-lang-identity {:total-unregistered 1, :note \"orgs/kotoba-lang/identity exists on disk, is the canonical provider for the :identity required-technology (167/175 blueprint consumers), but has zero entry in manifest/west.yml. Lower-risk, single-entry fix — no concurrent-loop conflict known.\"}}", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/required-technology-index "[{:capability :audit-ledger, :consumer-count 175, :consumer-fraction \"175/175 (universal)\", :canonical-provider nil, :status :gap, :note \"every single cloud-itonami blueprint declares this, but no kotoba-lang repo is literally named audit-ledger. The real substrate is scattered across kotoba-lang/{commit-dag,prolly-tree,kotobase-peer} + kotoba's own Datom log (ADR-2607022600 database-crates roadmap). Highest-value single fix: either register one of these as the canonical `:audit-ledger` referent in blueprint READMEs, or scaffold a thin kotoba-lang/audit-ledger contract repo that composes them, matching the pattern kotoba-lang/industry plays for :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5.\"} {:capability :bpmn, :consumer-count 170, :consumer-fraction \"170/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/bpmn\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :duplicate-found, :note \"com-junkawasaki/bpmn-clj exists locally (untracked, unregistered), src tree BYTE-IDENTICAL (diff -rq: no differences) to kotoba-lang/bpmn. This is the ADR-2606302300 -clj-migration leftover, same shape as the kototama-clj case ADR-2607022800 Phase 5 retired. Candidate for the same retirement treatment, pending owner confirmation (not done by this ADR).\"} {:capability :forms, :consumer-count 168, :consumer-fraction \"168/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/forms\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :clean} {:capability :identity, :consumer-count 167, :consumer-fraction \"167/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/identity\", :provider-registered-in-west false, :status :west-registration-gap, :note \"repo exists on disk at orgs/kotoba-lang/identity but has NO entry in manifest/west.yml at all — a plain registration gap, same category as the 5 repos ADR-2607022800 gap-swept, except this one is load-bearing for 167 of 175 blueprints' declared capability layer.\"} {:capability :dmn, :consumer-count 167, :consumer-fraction \"167/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/dmn\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :duplicate-found, :note \"com-junkawasaki/dmn-clj exists locally (untracked, unregistered), src tree BYTE-IDENTICAL to kotoba-lang/dmn. Same leftover-migration shape as bpmn above.\"} {:capability :robotics, :consumer-count 80, :consumer-fraction \"80/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/robotics\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :clean, :note \"the robotics premise is explicit in every blueprint's README (\\\"a robot performs the physical domain work\\\", governor gates hardware dispatch) — matches the owner's framing that cloud-itonami is fundamentally robotics/agent-automation for supply-chain actors, not a pure SaaS form-filler.\"} {:capability :telemetry, :consumer-count 10, :consumer-fraction \"10/175\", :canonical-provider nil, :status :gap, :note \"no kotoba-lang/telemetry repo exists at all. Declared but genuinely unbuilt.\"} {:capability :insurance, :consumer-count 7, :consumer-fraction \"7/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/insurance\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :clean} {:capability :securities, :consumer-count 5, :consumer-fraction \"5/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/securities\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :clean} {:capability :banking, :consumer-count 4, :consumer-fraction \"4/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/banking\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :clean} {:capability :optimization, :consumer-count 4, :consumer-fraction \"4/175 required + 1/175 optional\", :canonical-provider nil, :status :gap, :note \"no kotoba-lang/optimization repo. Genuinely unbuilt.\"} {:capability :property, :consumer-count 2, :consumer-fraction \"2/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/property\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :clean} {:capability :cae, :consumer-count 1, :consumer-fraction \"1/175 (cloud-itonami-7210)\", :canonical-provider nil, :status :open-question, :note \"no literal kotoba-lang/cae repo. kotoba-lang/cae-solver exists and is registered, but per ADR-2607022800's naming-collision table cae-solver is \\\"reduced-order vehicle CAE solver\\\", scoped to the aero/crash/datom/echem/motor/vphysics cluster — NOT confirmed to be the same capability this one blueprint means by generic :cae. Flagged, not resolved (same discipline as ADR-2607022800's :open-questions).\"}]", :adr/composition-with-org-taxonomy "{:org-taxonomy-answers \"WHERE does a new repo get created? (ADR-2606302300: what-kind-of-thing x for-whom)\", :capability-map-answers \"WHAT function does an existing repo provide or consume, and who else provides/consumes the SAME function across org boundaries?\", :orthogonality \"a repo's org placement does not change; this map is a cross-cutting index layered on top, keyed by capability id, pointing at repos in whichever org actually holds them (overwhelmingly kotoba-lang for providers, per its \\\"language substrate consumed by all orgs\\\" role)\", :cloud-itonami-not-a-6th-tier \"reaffirms ADR-2606302300's 2026-07-01 amendment: cloud-itonami is not a 5th/6th taxonomy tier, it is the public-repo home for one gftdcojp product line's blueprint fleet; this ADR treats it as a CONSUMER-side data source (175 uniform blueprint.edn manifests) precisely because that fleet happens to be the only org-wide corpus with machine-readable capability declarations today\", :precedent-this-generalizes \"the ADR-2607022800 follow-up (2026-07-04) that found gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka and kami-mangaka-page/render/text/scene were two unrelated things both called \\\"mangaka\\\" is exactly the class of cross-org confusion a capability-tag index is meant to make mechanically checkable instead of requiring an ad-hoc owner question each time\"}", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-04", :adr/follow-up-2026-07-04-isic-rename "{:trigger \"owner: \\\"cloud-itonami-isco-{code}, cloud-itonami-isic-{code} などになるようにしてね\\\"\", :corpus-size-correction {:this-adrs-original-scan 175, :actual-github-org-total 288, :gap [\"88 cloud-itonami-isco-* occupation blueprints (ADR-2607012000) — never locally checked out, entirely absent from this ADR's original :cloud-itonami-blueprint-inventory\" \"25 more ISIC letter-prefixed repos beyond the 2 (L6810/M6910) sampled locally\"], :corrected-isic-family-count 97, :invalidates \"this ADR's original maturity finding (\\\"only L6810/M6910 graduated past scaffold, letter-prefix correlates with graduation\\\") — that correlation was an artifact of an incomplete local sample, not a real pattern. The letter prefix was simply an ISIC section-letter disambiguation used inconsistently across the fleet, unrelated to maturity.\"}, :renamed {:total 97, :method \"gh repo rename, zero collisions, zero failures\", :pattern \"cloud-itonami-{code} | cloud-itonami-{SectionLetter}{code} -> cloud-itonami-isic-{code}\", :internal-refs-fixed \"blueprint.edn + README.md + any docs/* file containing the literal old repo-name string, replaced and pushed in the same commit as each rename\", :l6810-self-id-fix \"cloud-itonami-L6810's blueprint.edn :itonami.blueprint/id already said \\\"cloud-itonami-6810\\\" (no L) BEFORE this rename -- the literal-string replacement correctly skipped it (never contained \\\"cloud-itonami-L6810\\\"); fixed with one direct follow-up edit to \\\"cloud-itonami-isic-6810\\\", now consistent\"}, :kotoba-lang-industry-registry-fix {:file \"orgs/kotoba-lang/industry/resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn\", :finding \"84 entries (:maturity :blueprint or :implemented) had :repo/:business-id pointing at the stale gftdcojp org; 12 of those also silently dropped the ISIC section-letter, pointing at URLs that never existed (e.g. id \\\"6310\\\" -> gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-6310, real repo was cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-J6310)\", :safety-check \"industry.cljc treats :repo/:business-id as opaque metadata (maturity only checks (boolean (:repo industry))); industry_test.clj asserts exclusively by ISIC :id, never by repo-name string\", :fix \"all 84 updated to https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-{id} / cloud-itonami-isic-{id}\", :test-result \"7 tests / 52 assertions, 0 failures, before and after\", :commit \"kotoba-lang/industry@67f8dd8\"}, :found-not-fixed {:phantom-repo-entries {:count 341, :of-total 425, :note \"425 registry entries have non-nil :repo; only 84 correspond to a real GitHub repo. 328 of the 341 phantom entries are explicitly :maturity :spec (registry.cljc's own docstring: :spec means \\\"registry only\\\", no repo) yet still carry a populated :repo URL -- contradicts the registry's own documented semantics. Pre-existing, unrelated to naming, NOT fixed by this follow-up -- flagged for whoever next audits kotoba-lang/industry.\"}, :registry-freshness-gap {:count 13, :note \"13 of the 97 real ISIC-family repos aren't referenced with a real maturity tier in the registry at all yet -- registry hasn't caught up to their creation, a freshness gap not a naming one\"}, :cae-question \"question 2 (:cae -> cae-solver correspondence) untouched, remains genuinely open\"}, :superproject-side-effect {:finding \"manifest/west.yml's kami-engine pin (d432d79) was found stale/behind the local checkout + remote main (abfeb2c) while trying to push the industry fix -- the west-pin-verify-guard hook blocks ALL git push commands until this is corrected, regardless of which repo is being pushed\", :fix \"nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry kami-engine, verified OK, single-line pin correction\", :unrelated-to-capability-map \"pre-existing manifest staleness, not caused by or related to the ISIC rename work; fixed only because it was blocking unrelated pushes\"}}", :adr/cloud-itonami-blueprint-inventory "{:total-local-dirs 175, :naming-schemes {:plain-4-digit-isic 70, :letter-prefixed-isic [\"cloud-itonami-L6810\" \"cloud-itonami-M6910\"], :cofog-coded 5, :unspsc-segment-coded 5, :iso3166-country-or-agency-coded \"~80 (see ADR-2607040800/2607042900 — actively growing family, 71/193 countries + 19/19 Japan agencies at last count)\", :gtin-family 3}, :maturity {:public-oss-scaffold-only 173, :implemented-or-actively-developed 2, :implemented-repos [{:repo \"cloud-itonami-L6810\", :isic \"6810\", :domain \"real-estate agency\", :evidence \"real git history (\\\"feat: implement Realtor-LLM ⊣ RealtorGovernor closing-execution actor\\\", operator-console HTML sample), has src/test/deps.edn unlike the scaffold-only majority, blueprint.edn carries :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented\", :anomaly \"blueprint.edn's own :itonami.blueprint/id field says \\\"cloud-itonami-6810\\\" — NOT \\\"cloud-itonami-L6810\\\" — a self-id/dirname/remote-name mismatch. Flagged in :open-questions, not fixed (this is the single most actively-developed repo in the fleet; touching its identity is exactly the kind of thing that should get an explicit owner nod first).\"} {:repo \"cloud-itonami-M6910\", :isic \"6910\", :domain \"legal/company-formation (Global Incorporation Actor)\", :evidence \"real git history (\\\"fix: :application/intake ... could fabricate a fully filed company\\\", iterative-hardening commits)\", :self-id-consistent true, :note \"unlike L6810, M6910's :itonami.blueprint/id correctly says \\\"cloud-itonami-M6910\\\" — its own dirname/remote/id all agree. The only irregularity is the capital-letter prefix itself, shared with L6810 but not explained by any ADR found; empirically it correlates with \\\"graduated past scaffold\\\" rather than any ISIC-taxonomy convention (the other ISIC Section L/M divisions in this fleet, e.g. 7010/7210/7320, use plain digits with no letter).\"}]}, :status-field \"175/175 declare :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss; :itonami.blueprint/license 175/175 AGPL-3.0-or-later\"}", :db/id -1, :adr/forward-looking-gap "{:trigger \"owner clarification: cloud-itonami の本質は robotics / agent 自動化で、サプライチェーン企業が情報を載せ AI が分析・マッチングする\", :searched [\"kotoba-lang/*/README.md for matching|marketplace|supply-chain|supply chain\" \"manifest/repos.edn for the same terms\"], :found \"zero existing repos or :required-technology keywords covering AI-driven supply-chain data intake / cross-party matching\", :interpretation \"the :robotics required-technology (80/175 blueprints) covers the PHYSICAL execution premise (a robot/actor does the domain work under a governor), but there is no equivalent named capability yet for the DATA side the owner is describing — ingesting multi-party supply-chain listings and running AI matching/analysis over them. This is a genuine forward-looking gap, not a duplication or naming problem: nothing to consolidate, something to eventually design (candidate shape: a kotoba-lang vertical-capability-lib alongside banking/insurance/securities, e.g. :supply-chain-matching, consumed by whichever cloud-itonami blueprints need multi-party data intake — ISIC divisions like wholesale trade (46xx), logistics (52xx), or the KAMI provider-split's :giemon robot line are the most plausible first consumers).\", :not-scoped-to-this-adr \"no repo scaffolded, no ADR filed for it — recorded here as a data point for whoever next works on cloud-itonami's roadmap\"}", :adr/method "{:step1 \"babashka script read+edn/read-string every orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-*/blueprint.edn (175 dirs, 175 files, 0 parse errors)\", :step2 \"frequency-count :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies and :optional-technologies across all 175\", :step3 \"for each keyword, test directory existence of orgs/kotoba-lang/<kw> and orgs/com-junkawasaki/{<kw>,<kw>-clj}, then grep manifest/west.yml for registration of whichever exists\", :step4 \"byte-diff any keyword resolving to BOTH a kotoba-lang repo and a com-junkawasaki -clj repo, to distinguish genuine duplication from a completed-but-uncleaned migration\", :caveat \"point-in-time snapshot (2026-07-04); does not re-run automatically; the iso3166 sub-family in particular is a known-active /loop target (ADR-2607042900) and will have moved on by the time this is read\"}", :adr/open-questions "[{:q \"cloud-itonami-L6810's blueprint.edn self-identifies as \\\"cloud-itonami-6810\\\", disagreeing with its own directory name and GitHub remote (cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-L6810)\", :impact \"none for west/CI today (this repo is not yet west-registered at all — see :west-registration-gap); purely a latent trap for whoever registers or renames it next\", :suggested-fix \"owner call: either rename the repo/remote to drop the stray L (matching its own self-declared id and the other 173 plain-digit-ISIC blueprints), or correct the blueprint.edn id field to match the existing L6810 name — NOT both attempted silently, since this is the fleet's only :implemented repo with real git history\"} {:q \":cae required-technology (cloud-itonami-7210) has no literal kotoba-lang/cae provider; kotoba-lang/cae-solver exists but is documented elsewhere as a different, narrower thing (reduced-order vehicle CAE solvers)\", :impact \"none currently — a single blueprint, not yet west-registered\", :suggested-fix \"confirm with the blueprint's own README/domain (ISIC 7210 = R&D natural sciences) whether it actually means kotoba-lang/cae-solver, or needs its own general-CAE capability lib\"} {:q \"why do only cloud-itonami-L6810 and -M6910 carry a capital-letter prefix, when they are also the only two blueprints that graduated past scaffold to real implementation — is the letter prefix a deliberate (if undocumented) \\\"graduated\\\" marker, an ISIC-section-letter convention applied inconsistently, or coincidental?\", :impact \"none currently (naming-only)\", :suggested-fix \"none required; noted so a future batch-registration pass does not assume all 175 dirs follow one clean regex\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/scope "{:orgs-covered 5, :cloud-itonami-blueprint-dirs-scanned 175, :blueprint-edn-parsed 175, :required-technology-keywords-found 13, :duplicate-pairs-found 2, :west-registration-gaps-found 176}", :adr/title "ADR-2607051300: cross-org capability map (kotoba-lang / com-junkawasaki / gftdcojp / etzhayyim / cloud-itonami)"}]